BT /F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 717 Tm (Item 3. Access management standard) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 700 Tm (The Chief Information Security Officer presented version 4.0 of the access management standard, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 686.5 Tm (is milestone M1 of the remediation plan for MRA-PAM-05. Version 4.0 sets a deadline of one business) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 673 Tm (day for removing a leaver's access, requires each platform owner to review every privileged account each) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 659.5 Tm (quarter, requires reviewers to be trained before they review, and sets rules for orphaned accounts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 641 Tm (The committee asked whether one business day could be met for contractors, who are not in the HR) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 627.5 Tm (system. The Chief Information Security Officer said that the contractor management team would notify the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 614 Tm (identity team on each contractor's last day, as section 4.2 of the standard requires.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 595.5 Tm (Decision: the committee approved version 4.0 of the access management standard on 2026-03-26, with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 582 Tm (effect from 2026-04-01.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 40 Tm (Board Risk Committee, minutes of the meeting of 2026-03-26 - page 2 of 3) Tj ET
